  "query_preview": "..\nA minor trade-wind trough brought isolated showers to the region\ntoday. Tonight, a stronger trade-wind trough extending from an active\nsegment of the Near-Equatorial Trough (NET) to the south is expected\nto bring scattered showers to the region with slightly higher \nchances for Guam and Rota. Upper-level divergence paired with\nrelatively dry mid-level air may give way to a few thunderstorms, \nbut will mainly be concentrated over the southern half of the \nMarianas. Lingering scattered showers will continue for Guam and Rota\nFriday before clearing out and returning to 20 percent chances of\nshowers throughout the rest of the forecast period. The zones were\nsplit due to the short-term forecast differences, so they may be\ncombined again over the next few updates.",
